          <msContents>
            <summary>Account of receipts of rent from various manors in the Sandwich area of Kent. Containing on f. 107v 'Probata medicina ffor pe ffrenche poxe', probably written about 1503. This recipe for a cure for syphilis is at the back of an entry dated 1503 recording a payment by John Langley, gentleman of Knowlton in Kent, to the 'Pryncipall of Staple Yard in Holborn in London'. Above the prescription is a short musical composition on a five-line stave. </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">English</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_399_1">
              <author>Langley, John</author>
              <title type="original">Rental accounts, Kent</title>
              <title type="standard"/>
              <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">English</textLang>
              <filiation/>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
